;; Strict, idiom-focused clj-kondo config. See README ("Linting") and
;; doc-1 (Agentic Clojure Tooling Stack) for why clj-kondo was chosen.
;;
;; Every :level :warning entry below is OFF in clj-kondo's own defaults and
;; was individually confirmed (against this project's clj-kondo version) to
;; actually fire before being added here -- see TASK-34 notes for the
;; per-rule verification. Rules intentionally left disabled, with why:
;;
;; - :consistent-alias -- requires pre-declaring the canonical alias for
;;   every namespace up front (:aliases {ns alias, ...}). Premature for a
;;   fresh skeleton with no established aliasing conventions yet; revisit
;;   once real code settles on recurring requires.
;; - :redundant-fn-wrapper, :not-nil? -- could not get either to fire on
;;   their documented trigger patterns with this clj-kondo version, so they
;;   were left out rather than shipping unverified/dead config.
{:linters {:missing-docstring {:level :warning}
           :shadowed-var {:level :warning}
           :used-underscored-binding {:level :warning}
           :single-key-in {:level :warning}
           :unsorted-required-namespaces {:level :warning}
           :unused-alias {:level :warning}
           :equals-nil {:level :warning}
           :equals-true {:level :warning}
           :equals-false {:level :warning}
           :main-without-gen-class {:level :warning}}}
